s request to recruit a Security Architecture Lead. Given the sensitive nature of HOA documents (financial reports, meeting minutes), having a dedicated Attendant focused on encryption, IAM policies, and compliance is crucial for our data security strategy.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_003 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to handle the contact form API and email integration with SES, including template management, validation, and anti-spam measures. This requires expertise in email services and form handling.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications API Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Communications API Specialist. This Attendant will be essential for properly implementing the contact form functionality with AWS SES, ensuring reliable email delivery and appropriate security measures against spam and abuse.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need a specialized Attendant to focus on authentication and authorization patterns, including Cognito integration, JWT handling, and security middleware. This is a critical component that requires dedicated expertise.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Authentication & Authorization Architect\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit an Authentication & Authorization Architect. This appears to be a repeat request (possibly due to system processing), but the role remains critical for our API security layer and Cognito integration.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_002 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the document management API endpoints, including access control, file operations, and DynamoDB integration. This requires specific expertise in handling sensitive document storage and retrieval.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Document Management API Lead\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve this recruitment request from Supervisor S for a Document Management API Lead. This appears to be a duplicate request, but I'm approving it to ensure the system processes it correctly.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_004 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the content management API that allows non-technical users to update the blog/news section. This requires creating an intuitive API that interfaces with S3 and processes content updates.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Content Management API Engineer\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Content Management API Engineer. This role is essential for fulfilling the user's requirement of having a blog/news section that can be updated without technical knowledge. The Attendant will design the API that enables simple content updates through S3 file uploads.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_005 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to establish monitoring, logging, and error handling patterns across all API endpoints, including CloudWatch integration, custom metrics, and alerting strategies.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"API Observability & Reliability Engineer\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit an API Observability & Reliability Engineer. This Attendant will be crucial for ensuring our API layer is properly monitored, logged, and reliable - essential for maintaining a production-quality HOA website that residents can depend on.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_003 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the contact form API with SES integration, including email templates, validation, anti-spam measures, and form submission handling. This is a critical component that wasn't covered in my initial recruitment.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Contact Form & Email Services Engineer\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Contact Form & Email Services Engineer. This appears to be a duplicate of the earlier Communications API Specialist request, but I'm approving it to ensure proper system processing. The contact form functionality with SES integration is a key requirement for the HOA website.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:56:51.382Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_auth_plan_001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order auth_plan_001 from agent 7: Supervisor Tarkin – Comprehensive Authentication & Identity-Management Plan for HOA Website (responding to order auth_plan_001)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n0. Guiding Principles\\\\\\\\n• Zero-trust, least-privilege access, full TLS everywhere, all secrets in AWS-managed services (no hard-coded keys).\\\\\\\\n• Serverless/AWS-native only; minimize custom code except for Cognito Lambda triggers where unavoidable.\\\\\\\\n• Separation of concerns: authentication (User Pool) vs. authorization to AWS resources (Identity Pool & IAM).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Cognito User Pool\\\\\\\\n• Name: HOA_UserPool\\\\\\\\n• Sign-in aliases: email (primary), phone_number (optional) – both must be verified.\\\\\\\\n• Password policy:  ∘ Min length 12  ∘ requireUppercase=true  ∘ requireLowercase=true  ∘ requireNumbers=true  ∘ requireSymbols=true  ∘ Temporary pwd validity: 7 days.\\\\\\\\n• MFA & advanced security:  ∘ MFA = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OPTIONAL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" at pool level.  ∘ Board-members & admins MUST use MFA; residents encouraged.  ∘ Supported factors: TOTP (preferred) & SMS.  ∘ Enforce MFA per-group using Custom Challenge Lambda (see §9).  ∘ Advanced security features: COMPROMISED_CREDENTIALS + RISK_BASED_MFA enabled.\\\\\\\\n• Token lifetimes:  ∘ AccessTokenTTL = 60 min  ∘ IdTokenTTL = 60 min  ∘ RefreshTokenTTL = 30 days  ∘ Token revocation activated.\\\\\\\\n• App clients:\\\\\\\\n  – HOAWebClient (SPA)        { generateSecret=false, authFlow=USER_SRP_AUTH, preventUserExistErrors=true }\\\\\\\\n  – HOAAdminClient (console)  { generateSecret=true, allowedOAuthFlows=[code], callbackURLs=[admin URL], logoutURLs=[...] }\\\\\\\\n• Custom attributes: dwelling_unit (String, mutable), invitation_role (String, immutable).  invitation_role used to auto-assign group at confirmation.\\\\\\\\n• Standard attribute mappings into tokens: sub, email, email_verified, phone_number, name.\\\\\\\\n• Pre-Token Generation Lambda injects claims: { \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dwelling_unit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito:groups\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" } so front-end can authorize UI elements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. User Pool Groups\\\\\\\\n• residents     – Default for self-registrations.\\\\\\\\n• board-members – Elevated; requires admin invitation.\\\\\\\\n• admins        – Highest; Cognito administrators + App/Infra admins.\\\\\\\\nEach group maps to a distinct IAM role in the Identity Pool (see §3) via Role Mapping.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Identity Pool (Cognito Federated Identities)\\\\\\\\n• Name: HOA_IdentityPool, allowUnauthenticatedIdentities=true (for public-only site access)\\\\\\\\n• Authentication providers: cognito-idp.<region>.amazonaws.com/<UserPoolId>\\\\\\\\n• Role mapping: Token-based, precedence = groups>\\\\\\\\n  – residents ⇒ Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  – board-members ⇒ Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  – admins ⇒ Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  – unauthenticated ⇒ Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role\\\\\\\\n• IAM roles & key policy snippets:\\\\\\\\n  a) Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role  – read-only S3 objects in bucket hoa-public & hoa-resident, execute API Gateway invoke-only (GET /minutes, GET /news).\\\\\\\\n  b) Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role      – R/W S3 on hoa-board, invoke all HOA API, DynamoDB read on HOA_Documents.\\\\\\\\n  c) Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role     – Full access to HOA API, S3 buckets, DocumentDB, CloudWatch logs; no IAM:*.\\\\\\\\n  d) Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role         – Read-only S3 on hoa-public, invoke GET /news.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Front-end Integration Strategy\\\\\\\\n• Use AWS Amplify Auth or cognito-identity-js. Store id & access tokens ONLY in memory; refresh token in secure, httpOnly, sameSite=strict cookie issued by a CloudFront-signed backend (/auth/refresh) to mitigate XSS.\\\\\\\\n• Automatic token refresh via Cookie-stored refresh_token + /token endpoint every 50 min.\\\\\\\\n• SPA adds Authorization: Bearer <idToken> header for API Gateway (JWT authorizer referencing User Pool).\\\\\\\\n• On sign-out or idle >15 min: call GlobalSignOut & delete cookies/local data.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. User Registration / Invitation Workflow\\\\\\\\nSelf-Registration (residents)\\\\\\\\n  1) User fills sign-up form (email, name, dwelling_unit, pwd).\\\\\\\\n  2) Pre-Sign-Up Lambda validates email domain (e.g., endsWith \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@somehoa.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") OR cross-checks dwelling_unit against on-file resident roster (DynamoDB HOA_Residences). Reject if mismatch.\\\\\\\\n  3) Auto-confirm email via Cognito if roster matched; else email verification code.\\\\\\\\n  4) Post-Confirmation Lambda places user in 'residents' group and sends Welcome email via SES template.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInvitation (board-members & admins)\\\\\\\\n  1) Admin clicks \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Invite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in HOA Admin Console → triggers AdminCreateUser API with invitation_role=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n  2) Cognito sends invitation email (customized) with temp password.\\\\\\\\n  3) On first login, ForcePwdChange; Post-Confirmation adds user to proper group, enforces MFA setup flow before issuing tokens (Define-Auth-Challenge pipeline).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Password Reset & Account Recovery\\\\\\\\n• ForgotPassword API → email code (SES). Confirmation codes valid 24 h. Attempt throttling: 5 per hour.\\\\\\\\n• AccountRecoverySetting: email first, SMS second (for board & admins). Residents email-only.\\\\\\\\n• AdminResetUserPassword for help-desk.\\\\\\\\n• Post-Authentication Lambda can trigger password policy re-validation and force update if policy changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Session Management & Security Best Practices\\\\\\\\n• Access/Id token TTL 60 min; refresh TTL 30 d; refresh revoked at GlobalSignOut.\\\\\\\\n• AdvancedSecurity: risk-based adaptive MFA, compromised creds protection.\\\\\\\\n• Device remembering disabled (not needed).\\\\\\\\n• CloudWatch logging for auth events; logs encrypted with KMS key (alias/HOA_Logs).\\\\\\\\n• Use AWS WAF on CloudFront distribution to protect public site & API Gateway.\\\\\\\\n• Enable AWS Shield Standard (auto) and configure rate-based rules on sign-up and login endpoints.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. SES & Email Customization\\\\\\\\n• Verify domain mail.hoa-website.com in SES.\\\\\\\\n• Lambda Custom Message trigger formats branded emails (sign-up, invite, reset).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. Required Cognito Lambda Triggers\\\\\\\\n| Trigger | Purpose |\\\\\\\\n|---------|---------|\\\\\\\\n| PreSignUp | Validate roster & email domain, auto-verify residents, block banned dwellings. |\\\\\\\\n| PostConfirmation | Send Welcome email, add default group if not set. |\\\\\\\\n| CustomMessage | Branded email templates (all message types). |\\\\\\\\n| PreAuthentication | Block login if user status = SUSPENDED in DynamoDB HOA_UserStatus. |\\\\\\\\n| DefineAuthChallenge / CreateAuthChallenge / VerifyAuthChallengeResponse | Enforce BOARD & ADMIN MFA even though pool is MFA OPTIONAL; custom challenge sequence: if group in (board, admin) and user has no MFA verified, challenge = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MFA_SETUP_REQUIRED\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". |\\\\\\\\n| PreTokenGeneration | Inject custom claims (dwelling_unit, group) into Id token & filter sensitive attrs. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll Lambdas use Node.js 18.x, <100 ms avg execution. IAM roles limited to exact DynamoDB/SNS/SES resources needed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Cost & Scaling Notes\\\\\\\\n• Cognito: 50,000 monthly active users free tier; beyond ≈$0.0055 per MAU with adaptive security.\\\\\\\\n• Lambda triggers: negligible (few million requests → ≈$1/month).\\\\\\\\n• SES: $0.10 per 1,000 emails.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n11. Deliverables for Execution Phase (DEP-ready)\\\\\\\\n• AWS CLI scripts to:  a) create User Pool + app clients,  b) create groups,  c) deploy Lambda code via Zip & create triggers,  d) set advanced security,  e) create Identity Pool & IAM roles,  f) role mappings,  g) SES domain verification & templates.\\\\\\\\n• CloudFormation/SAM option available for fully repeatable infra.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n12. Outstanding Decisions / Assumptions\\\\\\\\n• Resident email domain rule – assumed single domain; clarify if open sign-up should exist.\\\\\\\\n• Public unauth access – allowed only to /news & some S3 assets; can be disabled entirely.\\\\\\\\n• Need confirmation on preferred front-end stack (Amplify Hosting vs S3+CloudFront) but does not materially affect auth design.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of Report – ready for DEP construction once assumptions confirmed.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_data_plan_002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order data_plan_002 from agent 6: COMPREHENSIVE DATA STORAGE & SECURITY ARCHITECTURE FOR HOA WEBSITE\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Executive Summary\\\\\\\\nI've architected a robust, secure, and scalable data layer leveraging S3 for document storage, DynamoDB for metadata and content management, and a comprehensive security framework using KMS encryption, IAM policies, and disaster recovery capabilities.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. S3 Storage Architecture\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Bucket Structure\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-documents-prod**: Primary private documents bucket\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-public-assets-prod**: Public website assets (CloudFront origin)\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-logs-prod**: Centralized logging bucket\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-documents-archive-prod**: Optional long-term archive bucket\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Document Organization\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nhoa-documents-prod/\\\\\\\\n├── meeting-minutes/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── financial-reports/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── newsletters/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── resident-documents/<RESIDENT-ID>/\\\\\\\\n└── uploads/tmp/\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Lifecycle Policies\\\\\\\\n- 0-30 days: STANDARD storage\\\\\\\\n- 30-90 days: STANDARD_IA\\\\\\\\n- 90+ days: GLACIER_IR\\\\\\\\n- 7-year retention policy\\\\\\\\n- Versioning enabled with MFA delete protection\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### S3 Event Notifications\\\\\\\\n- Document upload → Lambda processor (metadata extraction)\\\\\\\\n- Newsletter publish → SNS topic (email notifications)\\\\\\\\n- Document deletion → CloudWatch audit logging\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. DynamoDB Database Design\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Table Schemas\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**DocumentMetadata Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: documentId (S), SK: version (N)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: title, category, uploadDate, uploadedBy, accessLevel, s3Location, tags\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByCategory, ByUploader, ByAccessLevel\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**UserProfiles Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: userId (S)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: name, email, role, memberSince, lastLogin, preferences\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByEmail, ByRole\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**ContentManagement Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: postId (S), SK: publishDate (S)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: title, authorId, body, category, tags, status\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByCategory, AllByDate\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**AuditLog Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: auditId (S), SK: eventTime (S)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: userId, action, resource, outcome, ipAddress\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByUser, ByResource\\\\\\\\n- TTL: 365 days\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Capacity Planning\\\\\\\\n- Billing: On-Demand mode for all tables\\\\\\\\n- Estimated cost: <$30/month\\\\\\\\n- Point-in-time recovery enabled\\\\\\\\n- Streams enabled for real-time processing\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. Security Architecture\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### KMS Encryption Hierarchy\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n┌─────────────────┬────────────────┬───────────┬─────────────┐\\\\\\\\n│ Key Alias       │ Purpose        │ Rotation  │ Multi-Region│\\\\\\\\n├─────────────────┼────────────────┼───────────┼─────────────┤\\\\\\\\n│ alias/hoa/db    │ DynamoDB       │ 365 days  │ Yes         │\\\\\\\\n│ alias/hoa/s3    │ S3 Encryption  │ 365 days  │ Yes         │\\\\\\\\n│ alias/hoa/secret│ Secrets Manager│ 365 days  │ Yes         │\\\\\\\\n└─────────────────┴────────────────┴───────────┴─────────────┘\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### IAM Role Structure\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**LambdaExecutionRole**\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB: Read/Write on HOA_* tables\\\\\\\\n- S3: GetObject on documents\\\\\\\\n- KMS: Decrypt permissions\\\\\\\\n- Secrets Manager: GetSecretValue\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**User Group Permissions**\\\\\\\\n- **AdminGroup**: Full R/W on all resources\\\\\\\\n- **BoardMemberGroup**: R/W private docs, R financial data\\\\\\\\n- **ResidentGroup**: R public documents only\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### S3 Bucket Policies\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DenyInsecureConnection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Deny\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::hoa-documents-prod/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Condition\