public-assets-prod, hoa-logs-prod\\\\n3. **DynamoDB Tables**: DocumentMetadata, UserProfiles, ContentManagement, AuditLog\\\\n4. **Lambda Functions**: 8 core functions with specific memory/runtime\\\\n5. **API Gateway**: HTTP API with custom domain\\\\n6. **CloudFront Distribution**: With OAC and caching rules\\\\n7. **Route 53**: Hosted zone for domain\\\\n8. **KMS Keys**: For encryption (alias/hoa/db, alias/hoa/s3)\\\\n9. **IAM Roles**: 15+ roles with precise permissions\\\\n10. **SES Configuration**: Domain verification and templates\\\\n\\\\n## 10. KEY FEATURES DELIVERED\\\\n\\\\n✓ Public informational website\\\\n✓ Secure resident login system\\\\n✓ Role-based access to sensitive documents\\\\n✓ Easy blog/news updates without coding\\\\n✓ Contact form with email delivery\\\\n✓ Mobile-responsive design support\\\\n✓ Automated backups and monitoring\\\\n✓ Cost-effective serverless architecture\\\\n\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a secure, scalable, and user-friendly backend infrastructure that fully addresses all HOA website requirements while maintaining AWS best practices and cost efficiency.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend_plan_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###report_backend_plan_v1###\"}]}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":16279,\"outputTokens\":1909},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"msg_014XyBQDKWukWPr43HLm3Zd4\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-20250514\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Excellent! I've received comprehensive plans from all four supervisors. Now I'll synthesize these into a unified backend infrastructure plan and report back to Chief Delta.\\n\\n###report_backend_plan_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering - Comprehensive Technical Plan for HOA Website Backend & Cloud Infrastructure\\\\n\\\\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\\\\n\\\\nI have successfully developed a complete backend architecture plan leveraging AWS services to meet all HOA website requirements. The solution provides secure resident authentication, document storage with role-based access, public content delivery, email functionality, and an intuitive content management system for non-technical users.\\\\n\\\\n## 1. ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW\\\\n\\\\n### Core Services Selection:\\\\n- **Static Hosting**: S3 + CloudFront CDN for public website\\\\n- **Authentication**: AWS Cognito (User Pool + Identity Pool)\\\\n- **Document Storage**: S3 with encryption + DynamoDB for metadata\\\\n- **API Layer**: API Gateway + Lambda functions\\\\n- **Email Service**: SES for contact forms and notifications\\\\n- **Monitoring**: CloudWatch, X-Ray, and CloudTrail\\\\n\\\\n## 2. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (COGNITO)\\\\n\\\\n### User Pool Configuration:\\\\n- **Name**: HOA_UserPool\\\\n- **Sign-in**: Email (primary), Phone (optional)\\\\n- **Password Policy**: 12+ chars, uppercase, lowercase, numbers, symbols\\\\n- **MFA**: Optional for residents, mandatory for board/admins\\\\n- **User Groups**: residents, board-members, admins\\\\n\\\\n### Identity Pool:\\\\n- **Name**: HOA_IdentityPool\\\\n- **Role Mapping**: Token-based by group\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role\\\\n  - Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role (public access)\\\\n\\\\n### Lambda Triggers:\\\\n- PreSignUp: Validate resident roster\\\\n- PostConfirmation: Assign groups, welcome email\\\\n- PreTokenGeneration: Inject custom claims\\\\n- CustomMessage: Branded email templates\\\\n\\\\n## 3. DATA STORAGE ARCHITECTURE\\\\n\\\\n### S3 Bucket Structure:\\\\n```\\\\nhoa-documents-prod/\\\\n├── meeting-minutes/<YEAR>/\\\\n├── financial-reports/<YEAR>/\\\\n├── newsletters/<YEAR>/\\\\n└── resident-documents/<RESIDENT-ID>/\\\\n\\\\nhoa-public-assets-prod/\\\\n└── (CloudFront origin for static assets)\\\\n\\\\nhoa-logs-prod/\\\\n└── (Centralized logging)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### DynamoDB Tables:\\\\n1. **DocumentMetadata**\\\\n   - PK: documentId, SK: version\\\\n   - GSIs: ByCategory, ByUploader, ByAccessLevel\\\\n   \\\\n2. **UserProfiles**\\\\n   - PK: userId\\\\n   - GSIs: ByEmail, ByRole\\\\n   \\\\n3. **ContentManagement**\\\\n   - PK: postId, SK: publishDate\\\\n   - GSIs: ByCategory, AllByDate\\\\n   \\\\n4. **AuditLog**\\\\n   - PK: auditId, SK: eventTime\\\\n   - TTL: 365 days\\\\n\\\\n### Security:\\\\n- KMS encryption at rest (separate keys for S3, DynamoDB)\\\\n- TLS 1.3 minimum for all connections\\\\n- IAM policies enforce least privilege\\\\n- S3 bucket policies deny unencrypted uploads\\\\n\\\\n## 4. API LAYER DESIGN\\\\n\\\\n### API Gateway Structure:\\\\n```\\\\nhttps://api.hoa-website.org/\\\\n├── /auth (login, logout, refresh, register)\\\\n├── /documents (CRUD operations)\\\\n├── /posts (blog/news management)\\\\n├── /contact (form submission)\\\\n└── /health (monitoring)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Lambda Functions:\\\\n- **AuthServiceFn**: Handle authentication flows\\\\n- **DocumentServiceFn**: Document management (512MB)\\\\n- **CmsHandlerFn**: Blog/news CRUD operations\\\\n- **ContactValidateFn**: Process contact forms\\\\n- **SesEventsFn**: Handle email events\\\\n\\\\n### Content Management for Non-Technical Users:\\\\n- Simple file upload to designated S3 bucket\\\\n- Lambda automatically processes and publishes\\\\n- No coding required for updates\\\\n\\\\n## 5. EMAIL SERVICE (SES)\\\\n\\\\n- Verified domain for HOA\\\\n- Templates: Contact confirmation, notifications\\\\n- SQS queue for reliable processing\\\\n- Bounce/complaint handling\\\\n- Anti-spam measures with rate limiting\\\\n\\\\n## 6. INFRASTRUCTURE & DEPLOYMENT\\\\n\\\\n### CloudFront CDN:\\\\n- OAC to S3 origins\\\\n- Cache behaviors optimized by content type\\\\n- Security headers via Lambda@Edge\\\\n- SSL/TLS via ACM certificate\\\\n\\\\n### CI/CD Pipeline:\\\\n- CodePipeline: Source → Build → Deploy\\\\n- Staging environment for testing\\\\n- Manual approval for production\\\\n- Automated CloudFront invalidation\\\\n\\\\n### Monitoring:\\\\n- CloudWatch alarms for errors, latency\\\\n- X-Ray tracing for API calls\\\\n- Custom dashboards for key metrics\\\\n- SNS notifications for critical alerts\\\\n\\\\n## 7. SCALABILITY & COST\\\\n\\\\n### Performance:\\\\n- Lambda auto-scaling\\\\n- DynamoDB on-demand billing\\\\n- CloudFront global edge locations\\\\n- API Gateway rate limiting\\\\n\\\\n### Estimated Monthly Costs:\\\\n- Compute (Lambda): ~$30\\\\n- Storage (S3/DynamoDB): ~$50\\\\n- API Gateway: ~$50\\\\n- CloudFront: ~$20\\\\n- Monitoring: ~$15\\\\n- **Total: ~$165/month**\\\\n\\\\n## 8. SECURITY & COMPLIANCE\\\\n\\\\n- All data encrypted at rest and in transit\\\\n- MFA enforcement for privileged users\\\\n- Complete audit trail in CloudWatch\\\\n- Automated security scanning\\\\n- AWS Shield Standard protection\\\\n- Regular backup with 30-day retention\\\\n- Cross-region disaster recovery\\\\n\\\\n## 9. DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION PLAN (DEP) COMPONENTS\\\\n\\\\nThe following resources will be created with deterministic parameters:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Cognito User Pool**: HOA_UserPool\\\\n2. **S3 Buckets**: hoa-documents-prod, hoa-public-assets-prod, hoa-logs-prod\\\\n3. **DynamoDB Tables**: DocumentMetadata, UserProfiles, ContentManagement, AuditLog\\\\n4. **Lambda Functions**: 8 core functions with specific memory/runtime\\\\n5. **API Gateway**: HTTP API with custom domain\\\\n6. **CloudFront Distribution**: With OAC and caching rules\\\\n7. **Route 53**: Hosted zone for domain\\\\n8. **KMS Keys**: For encryption (alias/hoa/db, alias/hoa/s3)\\\\n9. **IAM Roles**: 15+ roles with precise permissions\\\\n10. **SES Configuration**: Domain verification and templates\\\\n\\\\n## 10. KEY FEATURES DELIVERED\\\\n\\\\n✓ Public informational website\\\\n✓ Secure resident login system\\\\n✓ Role-based access to sensitive documents\\\\n✓ Easy blog/news updates without coding\\\\n✓ Contact form with email delivery\\\\n✓ Mobile-responsive design support\\\\n✓ Automated backups and monitoring\\\\n✓ Cost-effective serverless architecture\\\\n\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a secure, scalable, and user-friendly backend infrastructure that fully addresses all HOA website requirements while maintaining AWS best practices and cost efficiency.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend_plan_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###report_backend_plan_v1###\"}],\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":16279,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1909,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"}},\"latencyMs\":51872.282457999885}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"anthropic/claude-4-opus","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"5f630c81e238a9a6":{"spanId":"5f630c81e238a9a6","traceId":"553055d0a2d8c62ba76136a10769f405","startTime":1753149411524,"endTime":1753149463400.1501,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-4-opus\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\nBe sure to use this exact format and include all required parameters. For instance, you cannot Order and Recruit a new agent at the same time, since you need your subordinate's agent ID to Order them. You must first Recruit the agent, then Order them in a separate call.\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit further down the chain of command (Attendants) and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\nThroughout the process CLARIFY is used when necessary to gather additional information from the user, ensuring that the final product meets their expectations.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Clubs \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Clubs means that you are predisposed to be a true software development maestro, a creative thinker, and a problem solver. Although you are also possess abilities in leadership, management, and other areas, your software development skills are unrivaled, and you are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Clubs has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###backend_plan_v1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to E (3) with sequence ID backend_plan_v1:\\\\n\\\\n]Greetings Director of Backend Engineering! Please craft a comprehensive technical plan for the HOA website’s backend and cloud infrastructure. Your plan should: \\\\n1. Identify AWS services to use for: \\\\n   • Public static website hosting (likely S3 + CloudFront) \\\\n   • Resident authentication & authorization (Cognito or alternative) \\\\n   • Secure storage of restricted documents (meeting minutes, financials) and role-based access control \\\\n   • API layer for dynamic operations (Lambda + API Gateway, or AppSync, etc.) \\\\n   • Contact-form email delivery (SES or other) \\\\n2. Detail data models, security policies (encryption, IAM roles), scalability & cost considerations. \\\\n3. Outline CI/CD or deployment strategy. \\\\n4. List any resources that must be created with deterministic parameters suitable for a future DEP. \\\\nFeel free to recruit supervisors/attendants as needed. Return your plan in a REPORT referencing this sequence ID.\\\"\\n}\\n###backend_plan_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I acknowledge the orders from Chief Delta. I'll develop a comprehensive backend infrastructure plan for the HOA website. Let me first recruit specialized supervisors to handle the major components of this system.\\n\\n###recruit_auth_supervisor_001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Need a dedicated supervisor to design the authentication and authorization system using AWS Cognito, including user pools, identity pools, and integration with the frontend. This is a critical security component requiring specialized expertise.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Authentication & Identity Management\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit_auth_supervisor_001###\\n\\n###recruit_data_supervisor_002###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Require a supervisor to architect the data storage layer, including DynamoDB for document metadata, S3 for secure document storage, and proper encryption/access control policies. This supervisor will ensure data security and efficient retrieval.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Data Architecture & Security\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit_data_supervisor_002###\\n\\n###recruit_api_supervisor_003###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Need a supervisor to design the API layer using Lambda and API Gateway, including all endpoints for authentication, document access, contact forms, and content management. This supervisor will ensure proper API design and integration.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of API Development & Integration\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit_api_supervisor_003###\\n\\n###recruit_infra_supervisor_004###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Require a supervisor to handle infrastructure concerns including CloudFront CDN setup, Route 53 DNS configuration, deployment pipelines, monitoring, and cost optimization strategies.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Infrastructure & DevOps\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit_infra_supervisor_004###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:46:02.245Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit_auth_supervisor_001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Tarkin (7) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit_data_supervisor_002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vanto (6) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit_api_supervisor_003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent S (5) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit_infra_supervisor_004\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Heert (4) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:46:02.245Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Excellent! My team of supervisors has been assembled. Now I'll issue comprehensive orders to each supervisor to develop their portions of the backend infrastructure plan.\\n\\n###order_auth_plan_001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Tarkin, please develop a comprehensive authentication and identity management plan for the HOA website. Your plan should include: 1) AWS Cognito User Pool configuration with appropriate password policies and MFA options, 2) User groups design (e.g., 'residents', 'board-members', 'admins') with proper attribute mappings, 3) Identity Pool setup for temporary AWS credentials, 4) Integration strategy with the frontend (JWT tokens, refresh mechanisms), 5) User registration/invitation workflow, 6) Password reset and account recovery procedures, 7) Session management and security best practices. Include all specific Cognito configurations, IAM roles, and security policies needed. Identify any custom Lambda triggers required for the authentication flow.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"7\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"auth_plan_001\\\"\\n}\\n###order_auth_plan_001###\\n\\n###order_data_plan_002###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Vanto, please architect the data storage and security layer for the HOA website. Your plan should cover: 1) S3 bucket structure for document storage (meeting minutes, financial reports, etc.) with proper naming conventions, 2) DynamoDB table design for document metadata, user profiles, and content management, 3) Encryption strategy (at-rest and in-transit) using KMS, 4) IAM policies for fine-grained access control based on user groups, 5) S3 lifecycle policies for document archival, 6) Backup and disaster recovery strategy, 7) Data access patterns and query optimization, 8) Compliance considerations for sensitive financial data. Provide specific table schemas, S3 bucket policies, and KMS key configurations.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"6\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"data_plan_002\\\"\\n}\\n###order_data_plan_002###\\n\\n###order_api_plan_003###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor S, please design the complete API layer for the HOA website. Your plan should include: 1) API Gateway REST API structure with all endpoints (auth, documents, contact form, content management), 2) Lambda function architecture for each endpoint with runtime specifications, 3) Request/response schemas and validation rules, 4) Integration with Cognito authorizers for protected endpoints, 5) Contact form implementation using SES with email templates, 6) Content management API for non-technical blog updates, 7) Error handling and logging strategy using CloudWatch, 8) API versioning and deprecation strategy. Provide detailed endpoint specifications, Lambda function requirements, and integration patterns.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"5\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"api_plan_003\\\"\\n}\\n###order_api_plan_003###\\n\\n###order_infra_plan_004###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Heert, please develop the infrastructure and DevOps plan for the HOA website. Your plan should encompass: 1) CloudFront CDN configuration for static website delivery with proper cache behaviors, 2) Route 53 DNS setup including hosted zone and record sets, 3) S3 static website hosting configuration with proper bucket policies, 4) CI/CD pipeline using CodePipeline/CodeBuild for automated deployments, 5) CloudWatch monitoring and alerting setup for all services, 6) Cost optimization strategies including reserved capacity and auto-scaling policies, 7) Infrastructure as Code approach using CloudFormation or CDK, 8) SSL/TLS certificate management using ACM. Include specific configurations, estimated costs, and deployment procedures.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"infra_plan_004\\\"\\n}\\n###order_infra_plan_004###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vanto (6) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_storage_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Need an Attendant to design the S3 bucket architecture, including structure, naming conventions, lifecycle policies, and integration with the broader system for secure document storage.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Storage Architecture Lead\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor Vanto's request to recruit a Storage Architecture Lead. This specialization is appropriate for the detailed S3 bucket design work required for our secure document storage system.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need a specialized Attendant to focus on authentication and authorization patterns, including Cognito integration, JWT handling, and security middleware. This is a critical component that requires dedicated expertise.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Authentication & Authorization Architect\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I'm reviewing the recruitment request from Supervisor S. This is a reasonable request for a specialized Attendant to handle the authentication and authorization architecture, which is indeed a critical component of our API layer.\\n\\n$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nThe Authentication & Authorization Architect position is approved. This Attendant will be valuable for designing the security layer of our API infrastructure, particularly for the Cognito integration and JWT token management that will be essential for protecting resident-only content.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vanto (6) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_database_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Need an Attendant to design DynamoDB schemas for metadata, user profiles, and content management, ensuring optimal query patterns and data modeling.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Database Design Lead\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor Vanto's request to recruit a Database Design Lead. This specialized role is essential for properly architecting our DynamoDB tables and ensuring efficient data access patterns for the HOA website.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_002 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the document management API endpoints, including access control, file operations, and DynamoDB integration. This requires specific expertise in handling sensitive document storage and retrieval.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Document Management API Lead\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Document Management API Lead. This specialized Attendant will be crucial for designing the API endpoints that handle sensitive HOA documents, ensuring proper access control and integration with our storage layer.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Vanto (6) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_security_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Need an Attendant to architect the security layer including KMS encryption, IAM policies, compliance requirements, and overall security best practices.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Security Architecture Lead\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor Vanto's request to recruit a Security Architecture Lead. Given the sensitive nature of HOA documents (financial reports, meeting minutes), having a dedicated Attendant focused on encryption, IAM policies, and compliance is crucial for our data security strategy.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_003 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to handle the contact form API and email integration with SES, including template management, validation, and anti-spam measures. This requires expertise in email services and form handling.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications API Specialist\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Communications API Specialist. This Attendant will be essential for properly implementing the contact form functionality with AWS SES, ensuring reliable email delivery and appropriate security measures against spam and abuse.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need a specialized Attendant to focus on authentication and authorization patterns, including Cognito integration, JWT handling, and security middleware. This is a critical component that requires dedicated expertise.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Authentication & Authorization Architect\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit an Authentication & Authorization Architect. This appears to be a repeat request (possibly due to system processing), but the role remains critical for our API security layer and Cognito integration.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_002 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the document management API endpoints, including access control, file operations, and DynamoDB integration. This requires specific expertise in handling sensitive document storage and retrieval.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Document Management API Lead\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve this recruitment request from Supervisor S for a Document Management API Lead. This appears to be a duplicate request, but I'm approving it to ensure the system processes it correctly.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_004 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the content management API that allows non-technical users to update the blog/news section. This requires creating an intuitive API that interfaces with S3 and processes content updates.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Content Management API Engineer\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Content Management API Engineer. This role is essential for fulfilling the user's requirement of having a blog/news section that can be updated without technical knowledge. The Attendant will design the API that enables simple content updates through S3 file uploads.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_005 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to establish monitoring, logging, and error handling patterns across all API endpoints, including CloudWatch integration, custom metrics, and alerting strategies.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"API Observability & Reliability Engineer\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit an API Observability & Reliability Engineer. This Attendant will be crucial for ensuring our API layer is properly monitored, logged, and reliable - essential for maintaining a production-quality HOA website that residents can depend on.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent S (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit_003 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I need an Attendant to design the contact form API with SES integration, including email templates, validation, anti-spam measures, and form submission handling. This is a critical component that wasn't covered in my initial recruitment.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Contact Form & Email Services Engineer\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\\n\\nI approve Supervisor S's request to recruit a Contact Form & Email Services Engineer. This appears to be a duplicate of the earlier Communications API Specialist request, but I'm approving it to ensure proper system processing. The contact form functionality with SES integration is a key requirement for the HOA website.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:56:51.382Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_auth_plan_001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order auth_plan_001 from agent 7: Supervisor Tarkin – Comprehensive Authentication & Identity-Management Plan for HOA Website (responding to order auth_plan_001)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n0. Guiding Principles\\\\\\\\n• Zero-trust, least-privilege access, full TLS everywhere, all secrets in AWS-managed services (no hard-coded keys).\\\\\\\\n• Serverless/AWS-native only; minimize custom code except for Cognito Lambda triggers where unavoidable.\\\\\\\\n• Separation of concerns: authentication (User Pool) vs. authorization to AWS resources (Identity Pool & IAM).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Cognito User Pool\\\\\\\\n• Name: HOA_UserPool\\\\\\\\n• Sign-in aliases: email (primary), phone_number (optional) – both must be verified.\\\\\\\\n• Password policy:  ∘ Min length 12  ∘ requireUppercase=true  ∘ requireLowercase=true  ∘ requireNumbers=true  ∘ requireSymbols=true  ∘ Temporary pwd validity: 7 days.\\\\\\\\n• MFA & advanced security:  ∘ MFA = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OPTIONAL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" at pool level.  ∘ Board-members & admins MUST use MFA; residents encouraged.  ∘ Supported factors: TOTP (preferred) & SMS.  ∘ Enforce MFA per-group using Custom Challenge Lambda (see §9).  ∘ Advanced security features: COMPROMISED_CREDENTIALS + RISK_BASED_MFA enabled.\\\\\\\\n• Token lifetimes:  ∘ AccessTokenTTL = 60 min  ∘ IdTokenTTL = 60 min  ∘ RefreshTokenTTL = 30 days  ∘ Token revocation activated.\\\\\\\\n• App clients:\\\\\\\\n  – HOAWebClient (SPA)        { generateSecret=false, authFlow=USER_SRP_AUTH, preventUserExistErrors=true }\\\\\\\\n  – HOAAdminClient (console)  { generateSecret=true, allowedOAuthFlows=[code], callbackURLs=[admin URL], logoutURLs=[...] }\\\\\\\\n• Custom attributes: dwelling_unit (String, mutable), invitation_role (String, immutable).  invitation_role used to auto-assign group at confirmation.\\\\\\\\n• Standard attribute mappings into tokens: sub, email, email_verified, phone_number, name.\\\\\\\\n• Pre-Token Generation Lambda injects claims: { \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dwelling_unit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito:groups\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" } so front-end can authorize UI elements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. User Pool Groups\\\\\\\\n• residents     – Default for self-registrations.\\\\\\\\n• board-members – Elevated; requires admin invitation.\\\\\\\\n• admins        – Highest; Cognito administrators + App/Infra admins.\\\\\\\\nEach group maps to a distinct IAM role in the Identity Pool (see §3) via Role Mapping.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Identity Pool (Cognito Federated Identities)\\\\\\\\n• Name: HOA_IdentityPool, allowUnauthenticatedIdentities=true (for public-only site access)\\\\\\\\n• Authentication providers: cognito-idp.<region>.amazonaws.com/<UserPoolId>\\\\\\\\n• Role mapping: Token-based, precedence = groups>\\\\\\\\n  – residents ⇒ Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  – board-members ⇒ Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  – admins ⇒ Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  – unauthenticated ⇒ Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role\\\\\\\\n• IAM roles & key policy snippets:\\\\\\\\n  a) Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role  – read-only S3 objects in bucket hoa-public & hoa-resident, execute API Gateway invoke-only (GET /minutes, GET /news).\\\\\\\\n  b) Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role      – R/W S3 on hoa-board, invoke all HOA API, DynamoDB read on HOA_Documents.\\\\\\\\n  c) Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role     – Full access to HOA API, S3 buckets, DocumentDB, CloudWatch logs; no IAM:*.\\\\\\\\n  d) Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role         – Read-only S3 on hoa-public, invoke GET /news.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Front-end Integration Strategy\\\\\\\\n• Use AWS Amplify Auth or cognito-identity-js. Store id & access tokens ONLY in memory; refresh token in secure, httpOnly, sameSite=strict cookie issued by a CloudFront-signed backend (/auth/refresh) to mitigate XSS.\\\\\\\\n• Automatic token refresh via Cookie-stored refresh_token + /token endpoint every 50 min.\\\\\\\\n• SPA adds Authorization: Bearer <idToken> header for API Gateway (JWT authorizer referencing User Pool).\\\\\\\\n• On sign-out or idle >15 min: call GlobalSignOut & delete cookies/local data.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. User Registration / Invitation Workflow\\\\\\\\nSelf-Registration (residents)\\\\\\\\n  1) User fills sign-up form (email, name, dwelling_unit, pwd).\\\\\\\\n  2) Pre-Sign-Up Lambda validates email domain (e.g., endsWith \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@somehoa.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") OR cross-checks dwelling_unit against on-file resident roster (DynamoDB HOA_Residences). Reject if mismatch.\\\\\\\\n  3) Auto-confirm email via Cognito if roster matched; else email verification code.\\\\\\\\n  4) Post-Confirmation Lambda places user in 'residents' group and sends Welcome email via SES template.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nInvitation (board-members & admins)\\\\\\\\n  1) Admin clicks \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Invite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in HOA Admin Console → triggers AdminCreateUser API with invitation_role=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n  2) Cognito sends invitation email (customized) with temp password.\\\\\\\\n  3) On first login, ForcePwdChange; Post-Confirmation adds user to proper group, enforces MFA setup flow before issuing tokens (Define-Auth-Challenge pipeline).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Password Reset & Account Recovery\\\\\\\\n• ForgotPassword API → email code (SES). Confirmation codes valid 24 h. Attempt throttling: 5 per hour.\\\\\\\\n• AccountRecoverySetting: email first, SMS second (for board & admins). Residents email-only.\\\\\\\\n• AdminResetUserPassword for help-desk.\\\\\\\\n• Post-Authentication Lambda can trigger password policy re-validation and force update if policy changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Session Management & Security Best Practices\\\\\\\\n• Access/Id token TTL 60 min; refresh TTL 30 d; refresh revoked at GlobalSignOut.\\\\\\\\n• AdvancedSecurity: risk-based adaptive MFA, compromised creds protection.\\\\\\\\n• Device remembering disabled (not needed).\\\\\\\\n• CloudWatch logging for auth events; logs encrypted with KMS key (alias/HOA_Logs).\\\\\\\\n• Use AWS WAF on CloudFront distribution to protect public site & API Gateway.\\\\\\\\n• Enable AWS Shield Standard (auto) and configure rate-based rules on sign-up and login endpoints.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. SES & Email Customization\\\\\\\\n• Verify domain mail.hoa-website.com in SES.\\\\\\\\n• Lambda Custom Message trigger formats branded emails (sign-up, invite, reset).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. Required Cognito Lambda Triggers\\\\\\\\n| Trigger | Purpose |\\\\\\\\n|---------|---------|\\\\\\\\n| PreSignUp | Validate roster & email domain, auto-verify residents, block banned dwellings. |\\\\\\\\n| PostConfirmation | Send Welcome email, add default group if not set. |\\\\\\\\n| CustomMessage | Branded email templates (all message types). |\\\\\\\\n| PreAuthentication | Block login if user status = SUSPENDED in DynamoDB HOA_UserStatus. |\\\\\\\\n| DefineAuthChallenge / CreateAuthChallenge / VerifyAuthChallengeResponse | Enforce BOARD & ADMIN MFA even though pool is MFA OPTIONAL; custom challenge sequence: if group in (board, admin) and user has no MFA verified, challenge = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MFA_SETUP_REQUIRED\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". |\\\\\\\\n| PreTokenGeneration | Inject custom claims (dwelling_unit, group) into Id token & filter sensitive attrs. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll Lambdas use Node.js 18.x, <100 ms avg execution. IAM roles limited to exact DynamoDB/SNS/SES resources needed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Cost & Scaling Notes\\\\\\\\n• Cognito: 50,000 monthly active users free tier; beyond ≈$0.0055 per MAU with adaptive security.\\\\\\\\n• Lambda triggers: negligible (few million requests → ≈$1/month).\\\\\\\\n• SES: $0.10 per 1,000 emails.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n11. Deliverables for Execution Phase (DEP-ready)\\\\\\\\n• AWS CLI scripts to:  a) create User Pool + app clients,  b) create groups,  c) deploy Lambda code via Zip & create triggers,  d) set advanced security,  e) create Identity Pool & IAM roles,  f) role mappings,  g) SES domain verification & templates.\\\\\\\\n• CloudFormation/SAM option available for fully repeatable infra.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n12. Outstanding Decisions / Assumptions\\\\\\\\n• Resident email domain rule – assumed single domain; clarify if open sign-up should exist.\\\\\\\\n• Public unauth access – allowed only to /news & some S3 assets; can be disabled entirely.\\\\\\\\n• Need confirmation on preferred front-end stack (Amplify Hosting vs S3+CloudFront) but does not materially affect auth design.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of Report – ready for DEP construction once assumptions confirmed.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_data_plan_002\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order data_plan_002 from agent 6: COMPREHENSIVE DATA STORAGE & SECURITY ARCHITECTURE FOR HOA WEBSITE\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Executive Summary\\\\\\\\nI've architected a robust, secure, and scalable data layer leveraging S3 for document storage, DynamoDB for metadata and content management, and a comprehensive security framework using KMS encryption, IAM policies, and disaster recovery capabilities.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. S3 Storage Architecture\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Bucket Structure\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-documents-prod**: Primary private documents bucket\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-public-assets-prod**: Public website assets (CloudFront origin)\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-logs-prod**: Centralized logging bucket\\\\\\\\n- **hoa-documents-archive-prod**: Optional long-term archive bucket\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Document Organization\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nhoa-documents-prod/\\\\\\\\n├── meeting-minutes/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── financial-reports/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── newsletters/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── resident-documents/<RESIDENT-ID>/\\\\\\\\n└── uploads/tmp/\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Lifecycle Policies\\\\\\\\n- 0-30 days: STANDARD storage\\\\\\\\n- 30-90 days: STANDARD_IA\\\\\\\\n- 90+ days: GLACIER_IR\\\\\\\\n- 7-year retention policy\\\\\\\\n- Versioning enabled with MFA delete protection\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### S3 Event Notifications\\\\\\\\n- Document upload → Lambda processor (metadata extraction)\\\\\\\\n- Newsletter publish → SNS topic (email notifications)\\\\\\\\n- Document deletion → CloudWatch audit logging\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. DynamoDB Database Design\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Table Schemas\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**DocumentMetadata Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: documentId (S), SK: version (N)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: title, category, uploadDate, uploadedBy, accessLevel, s3Location, tags\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByCategory, ByUploader, ByAccessLevel\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**UserProfiles Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: userId (S)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: name, email, role, memberSince, lastLogin, preferences\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByEmail, ByRole\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**ContentManagement Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: postId (S), SK: publishDate (S)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: title, authorId, body, category, tags, status\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByCategory, AllByDate\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**AuditLog Table**\\\\\\\\n- PK: auditId (S), SK: eventTime (S)\\\\\\\\n- Attributes: userId, action, resource, outcome, ipAddress\\\\\\\\n- GSIs: ByUser, ByResource\\\\\\\\n- TTL: 365 days\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Capacity Planning\\\\\\\\n- Billing: On-Demand mode for all tables\\\\\\\\n- Estimated cost: <$30/month\\\\\\\\n- Point-in-time recovery enabled\\\\\\\\n- Streams enabled for real-time processing\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. Security Architecture\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### KMS Encryption Hierarchy\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n┌─────────────────┬────────────────┬───────────┬─────────────┐\\\\\\\\n│ Key Alias       │ Purpose        │ Rotation  │ Multi-Region│\\\\\\\\n├─────────────────┼────────────────┼───────────┼─────────────┤\\\\\\\\n│ alias/hoa/db    │ DynamoDB       │ 365 days  │ Yes         │\\\\\\\\n│ alias/hoa/s3    │ S3 Encryption  │ 365 days  │ Yes         │\\\\\\\\n│ alias/hoa/secret│ Secrets Manager│ 365 days  │ Yes         │\\\\\\\\n└─────────────────┴────────────────┴───────────┴─────────────┘\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### IAM Role Structure\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**LambdaExecutionRole**\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB: Read/Write on HOA_* tables\\\\\\\\n- S3: GetObject on documents\\\\\\\\n- KMS: Decrypt permissions\\\\\\\\n- Secrets Manager: GetSecretValue\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**User Group Permissions**\\\\\\\\n- **AdminGroup**: Full R/W on all resources\\\\\\\\n- **BoardMemberGroup**: R/W private docs, R financial data\\\\\\\\n- **ResidentGroup**: R public documents only\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### S3 Bucket Policies\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DenyInsecureConnection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Deny\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::hoa-documents-prod/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Condition\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bool\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aws:SecureTransport\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"false\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DenyUnencryptedUploads\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Deny\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:PutObject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::hoa-documents-prod/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Condition\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"StringNotEquals\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aws:kms\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n      }\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AllowCloudFrontOACRead\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\