moDB\\\\\\\\n- Cross-region backup replication\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Disaster Recovery Plan\\\\\\\\n- **RTO**: 4 hours\\\\\\\\n- **RPO**: 1 hour\\\\\\\\n- S3 Cross-Region Replication to us-east-2\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB Global Tables for multi-region\\\\\\\\n- Multi-region KMS keys for seamless failover\\\\\\\\n- Quarterly DR drills scheduled\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 7. Compliance & Security Controls\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Compliance Alignment\\\\\\\\n- SOC 2 Type II controls implemented\\\\\\\\n- Data residency: US-only (us-east-1, us-east-2)\\\\\\\\n- Financial data encryption meets PCI-DSS requirements\\\\\\\\n- Full audit trail for compliance reporting\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Security Monitoring\\\\\\\\n- AWS GuardDuty enabled\\\\\\\\n- Security Hub for centralized findings\\\\\\\\n- CloudTrail logging all API calls\\\\\\\\n- AWS Config tracking configuration changes\\\\\\\\n- CloudWatch alarms for suspicious activities\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 8. Implementation Recommendations\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Infrastructure as Code**: Implement using AWS CDK or CloudFormation\\\\\\\\n2. **Phased Rollout**: \\\\\\\\n   - Phase 1: Core infrastructure (S3, DynamoDB, KMS)\\\\\\\\n   - Phase 2: Security policies and IAM\\\\\\\\n   - Phase 3: Backup and DR setup\\\\\\\\n   - Phase 4: Monitoring and compliance\\\\\\\\n3. **Testing Strategy**: Include security testing, performance testing, and DR simulations\\\\\\\\n4. **Cost Optimization**: Monitor with AWS Cost Explorer, implement tagging strategy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis architecture provides a secure, scalable, and maintainable data layer that meets all HOA website requirements while following AWS best practices for security, compliance, and operational excellence.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_api_plan_003\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order api_plan_003 from agent 5: ## Complete API Layer Design for HOA Website\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Executive Summary\\\\\\\\nI have successfully designed a comprehensive API layer for the HOA website that addresses all requirements: authentication, document management, contact forms, content management, and observability. The architecture leverages AWS services exclusively and provides a secure, scalable, and user-friendly solution.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 1. API Gateway Architecture\\\\\\\\n**Base Configuration:**\\\\\\\\n- Type: HTTP API (cost-effective, faster)\\\\\\\\n- Custom Domain: api.hoa-example.org\\\\\\\\n- Stages: dev, staging, prod\\\\\\\\n- CORS: Configured per endpoint\\\\\\\\n- Rate Limiting: 1000 req/min per IP\\\\\\\\n- WAF: Attached for security\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**API Structure:**\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nhttps://api.hoa-example.org/\\\\\\\\n├── /auth\\\\\\\\n│   ├── POST /login\\\\\\\\n│   ├── POST /logout\\\\\\\\n│   ├── POST /refresh\\\\\\\\n│   └── POST /register\\\\\\\\n├── /documents\\\\\\\\n│   ├── GET /documents (list)\\\\\\\\n│   ├── GET /documents/{id}\\\\\\\\n│   ├── POST /documents\\\\\\\\n│   └── DELETE /documents/{id}\\\\\\\\n├── /posts\\\\\\\\n│   ├── GET /posts (public)\\\\\\\\n│   ├── GET /posts/{id}\\\\\\\\n│   ├── POST /posts (admin)\\\\\\\\n│   ├── PUT /posts/{id}\\\\\\\\n│   ├── DELETE /posts/{id}\\\\\\\\n│   └── POST /posts/{id}/publish\\\\\\\\n├── /contact\\\\\\\\n│   └── POST /contact\\\\\\\\n├── /health\\\\\\\\n│   ├── GET /health\\\\\\\\n│   └── GET /health/deep\\\\\\\\n└── /rss\\\\\\\\n    └── GET /rss\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 2. Authentication & Authorization\\\\\\\\n**Cognito Configuration:**\\\\\\\\n- User Pool: HOAResidentsPool\\\\\\\\n- Custom Attributes: lotNumber, streetAddr, residentType, boardRole\\\\\\\\n- Groups: ResidentsGrp, BoardGrp, AdminGrp, CMS-Admin\\\\\\\\n- MFA: Optional (SMS/TOTP)\\\\\\\\n- Password Policy: 12+ chars, complexity required\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**JWT Authorization:**\\\\\\\\n- Custom API Gateway authorizer Lambda\\\\\\\\n- Token validation with JWKS caching\\\\\\\\n- Role-based access control (RBAC)\\\\\\\\n- Context injection for downstream Lambdas\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 3. Core Lambda Functions\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Authentication Services:**\\\\\\\\n- ApiJwtAuthorizerFn (256MB, Python 3.11)\\\\\\\\n- AuthServiceFn (handles login/logout/refresh)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Document Management:**\\\\\\\\n- DocumentServiceFn (512MB, Node.js 20)\\\\\\\\n- PresignUploadFn\\\\\\\\n- AntivirusScanFn (2GB, triggered by S3)\\\\\\\\n- OpenSearchIndexerFn (DynamoDB streams)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Content Management:**\\\\\\\\n- CmsHandlerFn (handles CRUD)\\\\\\\\n- ContentRenderFn (Markdown to HTML)\\\\\\\\n- RssGeneratorFn (SNS triggered)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Contact Form:**\\\\\\\\n- ContactValidateFn (256MB, Node.js 18)\\\\\\\\n- ContactEmailerFn (SQS triggered)\\\\\\\\n- SesEventsFn (handles bounces/complaints)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 4. Data Storage Design\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**DynamoDB Tables:**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **HOA_Documents**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: category, SK: documentId\\\\\\\\n   - GSI1: documentId-index\\\\\\\\n   - GSI2: uploadedBy-uploadedAt-index\\\\\\\\n   - Attributes: title, s3Key, fileType, etc.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. **BlogPosts**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: postId\\\\\\\\n   - GSI: status-publishedAt-index\\\\\\\\n   - Attributes: title, slug, status, content ref\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. **ContactEmailTxns**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: requestId\\\\\\\\n   - Tracks email delivery status\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**S3 Buckets:**\\\\\\\\n- hoa-docs-{env} (private documents)\\\\\\\\n- cms-content-{env} (blog content)\\\\\\\\n- Static assets served via CloudFront\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 5. Email Integration (SES)\\\\\\\\n- Verified domain: hoa-example.org\\\\\\\\n- Templates: Admin notification, User confirmation\\\\\\\\n- Configuration set with tracking\\\\\\\\n- SQS queue for reliable processing\\\\\\\\n- Bounce/complaint handling\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 6. Security Features\\\\\\\\n- WAF rules (geo-blocking, rate limiting)\\\\\\\\n- CAPTCHA integration for contact forms\\\\\\\\n- Input validation on all endpoints\\\\\\\\n- Presigned URLs for file operations\\\\\\\\n- IAM least privilege principles\\\\\\\\n- Secrets Manager for sensitive data\\\\\\\\n- SSE-S3 encryption for stored files\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 7. Monitoring & Observability\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**CloudWatch Configuration:**\\\\\\\\n- Structured JSON logging\\\\\\\\n- 30-day retention\\\\\\\\n- Custom metrics namespace: HOA/API\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Key Metrics:**\\\\\\\\n- API latency (p50, p95, p99)\\\\\\\\n- Error rates by endpoint\\\\\\\\n- Authentication success/failure\\\\\\\\n- Document upload/download counts\\\\\\\\n- Email delivery rates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Alarms:**\\\\\\\\n- High error rate (>10 in 5 min)\\\\\\\\n- High latency (p99 > 3s)\\\\\\\\n- Authentication failures spike\\\\\\\\n- SES bounce rate > 5%\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**X-Ray Tracing:**\\\\\\\\n- Full service map\\\\\\\\n- 100% sampling on errors\\\\\\\\n- Custom annotations\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 8. API Versioning Strategy\\\\\\\\n- Path-based versioning (/v1, /v2)\\\\\\\\n- Deprecation headers\\\\\\\\n- 6-month sunset period\\\\\\\\n- Migration guides\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 9. Non-Technical User Features\\\\\\\\n- Simple blog update via file upload\\\\\\\\n- Email-based notifications\\\\\\\\n- User-friendly error messages\\\\\\\\n- No coding required for content\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 10. Scalability & Performance\\\\\\\\n- Lambda concurrent execution limits\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB on-demand scaling\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront caching for static content\\\\\\\\n- SQS for async processing\\\\\\\\n- Connection pooling in Lambdas\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Cost Estimates (Monthly)\\\\\\\\n- API Gateway: ~$50\\\\\\\\n- Lambda executions: ~$30\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB: ~$25\\\\\\\\n- S3 & CloudFront: ~$20\\\\\\\\n- SES: ~$10\\\\\\\\n- Monitoring: ~$150\\\\\\\\n- **Total: ~$285/month**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Implementation Priority\\\\\\\\n1. Authentication infrastructure\\\\\\\\n2. Document management API\\\\\\\\n3. Contact form with email\\\\\\\\n4. Blog/content management\\\\\\\\n5. Monitoring setup\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Success Criteria\\\\\\\\n- All endpoints return <500ms p95 latency\\\\\\\\n- 99.9% uptime availability\\\\\\\\n- Zero security incidents\\\\\\\\n- Non-technical users can update content\\\\\\\\n- All sensitive data encrypted\\\\\\\\n- Complete audit trail\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis comprehensive API design provides a robust, secure, and user-friendly backend for the HOA website, fully leveraging AWS services while maintaining cost efficiency and scalability.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_infra_plan_004\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order infra_plan_004 from agent 4: Infrastructure & DevOps Plan for HOA Website:\\\\\\\\n1) CloudFront configuration: PriceClass_100, OAC to S3, default TTL 86400s, /assets/* TTL 1y, /index.html TTL 300s, Brotli/Gzip, security-headers Lambda@Edge, logs to dedicated bucket.\\\\\\\\n2) Route 53: public hosted zone 'hoaneighborhood.org', alias A/AAAA to CloudFront, optional www CNAME, MX if needed, DNSSEC enabled.\\\\\\\\n3) S3 static hosting: private buckets 'hoaneighborhood.org' (prod) and 'hoaneighborhood-staging', versioning and SSE-S3, bucket policy allows only CloudFront OAC, lifecycle rules to Glacier, access-logs bucket.\\\\\\\\n4) CI/CD: CodePipeline — Source(CodeCommit) → Build(CodeBuild, npm ci && npm run build) → Deploy(CodeBuild sync to S3 and invalidate CloudFront) with optional manual approval. Artifacts encrypted, 7-day retention.\\\\\\\\n5) Monitoring & alerting: CloudWatch alarms — CloudFront 5xx >1%, S3 4xx, pipeline failures, billing >25 USD; metrics dashboard; log retention 30 days then Glacier; SNS email alerts.\\\\\\\\n6) Cost optimisation: aggressive CloudFront caching, S3 Intelligent-Tiering for logs, BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL CodeBuild, 1-yr Savings Plan if Lambda grows, logs lifecycle. Estimated monthly cost ≈11–12 USD.\\\\\