B for metadata\\\\n- **API Layer**: API Gateway + Lambda functions\\\\n- **Email Service**: SES for contact forms and notifications\\\\n- **Monitoring**: CloudWatch, X-Ray, and CloudTrail\\\\n\\\\n## 2. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (COGNITO)\\\\n\\\\n### User Pool Configuration:\\\\n- **Name**: HOA_UserPool\\\\n- **Sign-in**: Email (primary), Phone (optional)\\\\n- **Password Policy**: 12+ chars, uppercase, lowercase, numbers, symbols\\\\n- **MFA**: Optional for residents, mandatory for board/admins\\\\n- **User Groups**: residents, board-members, admins\\\\n\\\\n### Identity Pool:\\\\n- **Name**: HOA_IdentityPool\\\\n- **Role Mapping**: Token-based by group\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role\\\\n  - Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role (public access)\\\\n\\\\n### Lambda Triggers:\\\\n- PreSignUp: Validate resident roster\\\\n- PostConfirmation: Assign groups, welcome email\\\\n- PreTokenGeneration: Inject custom claims\\\\n- CustomMessage: Branded email templates\\\\n\\\\n## 3. DATA STORAGE ARCHITECTURE\\\\n\\\\n### S3 Bucket Structure:\\\\n```\\\\nhoa-documents-prod/\\\\n├── meeting-minutes/<YEAR>/\\\\n├── financial-reports/<YEAR>/\\\\n├── newsletters/<YEAR>/\\\\n└── resident-documents/<RESIDENT-ID>/\\\\n\\\\nhoa-public-assets-prod/\\\\n└── (CloudFront origin for static assets)\\\\n\\\\nhoa-logs-prod/\\\\n└── (Centralized logging)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### DynamoDB Tables:\\\\n1. **DocumentMetadata**\\\\n   - PK: documentId, SK: version\\\\n   - GSIs: ByCategory, ByUploader, ByAccessLevel\\\\n   \\\\n2. **UserProfiles**\\\\n   - PK: userId\\\\n   - GSIs: ByEmail, ByRole\\\\n   \\\\n3. **ContentManagement**\\\\n   - PK: postId, SK: publishDate\\\\n   - GSIs: ByCategory, AllByDate\\\\n   \\\\n4. **AuditLog**\\\\n   - PK: auditId, SK: eventTime\\\\n   - TTL: 365 days\\\\n\\\\n### Security:\\\\n- KMS encryption at rest (separate keys for S3, DynamoDB)\\\\n- TLS 1.3 minimum for all connections\\\\n- IAM policies enforce least privilege\\\\n- S3 bucket policies deny unencrypted uploads\\\\n\\\\n## 4. API LAYER DESIGN\\\\n\\\\n### API Gateway Structure:\\\\n```\\\\nhttps://api.hoa-website.org/\\\\n├── /auth (login, logout, refresh, register)\\\\n├── /documents (CRUD operations)\\\\n├── /posts (blog/news management)\\\\n├── /contact (form submission)\\\\n└── /health (monitoring)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Lambda Functions:\\\\n- **AuthServiceFn**: Handle authentication flows\\\\n- **DocumentServiceFn**: Document management (512MB)\\\\n- **CmsHandlerFn**: Blog/news CRUD operations\\\\n- **ContactValidateFn**: Process contact forms\\\\n- **SesEventsFn**: Handle email events\\\\n\\\\n### Content Management for Non-Technical Users:\\\\n- Simple file upload to designated S3 bucket\\\\n- Lambda automatically processes and publishes\\\\n- No coding required for updates\\\\n\\\\n## 5. EMAIL SERVICE (SES)\\\\n\\\\n- Verified domain for HOA\\\\n- Templates: Contact confirmation, notifications\\\\n- SQS queue for reliable processing\\\\n- Bounce/complaint handling\\\\n- Anti-spam measures with rate limiting\\\\n\\\\n## 6. INFRASTRUCTURE & DEPLOYMENT\\\\n\\\\n### CloudFront CDN:\\\\n- OAC to S3 origins\\\\n- Cache behaviors optimized by content type\\\\n- Security headers via Lambda@Edge\\\\n- SSL/TLS via ACM certificate\\\\n\\\\n### CI/CD Pipeline:\\\\n- CodePipeline: Source → Build → Deploy\\\\n- Staging environment for testing\\\\n- Manual approval for production\\\\n- Automated CloudFront invalidation\\\\n\\\\n### Monitoring:\\\\n- CloudWatch alarms for errors, latency\\\\n- X-Ray tracing for API calls\\\\n- Custom dashboards for key metrics\\\\n- SNS notifications for critical alerts\\\\n\\\\n## 7. SCALABILITY & COST\\\\n\\\\n### Performance:\\\\n- Lambda auto-scaling\\\\n- DynamoDB on-demand billing\\\\n- CloudFront global edge locations\\\\n- API Gateway rate limiting\\\\n\\\\n### Estimated Monthly Costs:\\\\n- Compute (Lambda): ~$30\\\\n- Storage (S3/DynamoDB): ~$50\\\\n- API Gateway: ~$